---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Ref from '../../components/Ref.astro';
import { acts, inAct } from '../../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Stranger Than Heaven Acts and Cities: 1915 to 1965"
  description="The five acts of Stranger Than Heaven: Kokura 1915, Kure 1929, Osaka 1943, Atami 1951 and Shinjuku 1965. What is confirmed about each, and its achievements."
  path="/acts/"
>
  <h1>The five acts and their cities</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Stranger Than Heaven follows Makoto Daito for fifty years. Each act is a different city in a different decade
    <Ref ids="sega-0507" />.
  </p>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Act</th><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">In one line</th><th scope="col">Achievements</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {acts.map((act) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><a href={`/acts/${act.slug}/`}>Act {act.n}</a></th>
            <td>{act.year}</td>
            <td>{act.label}</td>
            <td>{act.setting[0].text}</td>
            <td>{inAct(act.n).length}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      SEGA describes the cities as a version of Japan inspired by real places of each period, not a recreation. The
      numbering of the acts comes from the <a href="/achievements/">achievement list</a>, which ties each act to a city
      by name: Kokura, Kure, Osaka, Atami and Shinjuku.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each act page gives what has been confirmed about the city, the characters tied to it, and the short list of
      achievements that belong to that act alone.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
